{"id": "housing-service-records-counted-twice", "title": "Housing office’s published service records: one in ten is a second copy", "seconds": 125.9, "voice": "elevenlabs:OUMCzFUTd0F4Q6lkLkco", "narrator": "Roxy", "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "76f8bb6e1e85e985", "words": 318, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "San Francisco’s housing office funds nonprofits to help people stay housed.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.8, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Mayor’s Office of Housing and Community Development", "sub": "eviction defence, rental assistance, case management"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.73, 1.12, 1.48, 1.96, 2.81, 2.97, 3.2, 3.56, 3.96]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "It publishes a record for every service, on the open-data portal.", "t0": 4.92, "t1": 8.31, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Mayor’s Office of Housing and Community Development", "sub": "eviction defence, rental assistance, case management"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.47, 0.57, 0.97, 1.21, 1.54, 2.22, 2.29, 2.4, 2.89]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["oneLine", "amount"], "text": "We read all 311,824 records, four years of them.", "t0": 8.43, "t1": 14.39, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "s1", "kicker": "DataSF dataset jy5g-rugu", "text": "311,824 service records, fiscal 2015-16 to 2018-19", "mark": "311,824"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.34, 0.57, 0.88, 1.22, 1.64, 2.31, 2.49, 2.9, 3.65, 4.66, 4.99, 5.37, 5.53]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["oneLine", "amount"], "text": "How many are second copies?", "t0": 14.39, "t1": 16.41, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "s1", "kicker": "DataSF dataset jy5g-rugu", "text": "311,824 service records, fiscal 2015-16 to 2018-19", "mark": "311,824"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.43, 0.6, 0.75, 1.05]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["oneLine", "amount"], "text": "33,114 records.", "t0": 16.41, "t1": 19.91, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "33,114", "label": "service records that are second copies", "sub": "66,228 records come in identical pairs"}, "emph": ["33,114"], "wt": [0.04, 0.68, 1.26, 1.56, 2.05, 2.71]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 20.43, "t1": 22.37, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.35, 0.49, 1.15, 1.39, 1.54]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]"], "text": "In 82 of 322 activity-years,", "t0": 22.59, "t1": 26.35, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "82 of 322 activity-years", "kicker": "The first lead", "sub": "same activity, year, age band, income band, race group, neighbourhood and client number"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.82, 1.14, 1.45, 1.78, 2.43]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]"], "text": "every record has an identical twin; in one, all but 4.", "t0": 26.35, "t1": 31.2, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "82 of 322 activity-years", "kicker": "The first lead", "sub": "same activity, year, age band, income band, race group, neighbourhood and client number"}, "emph": ["identical twin"], "wt": [0.04, 0.44, 0.93, 1.2, 1.3, 1.81, 2.8, 2.95, 3.85, 4.03, 4.31]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "Same activity, year, age, income, race group, neighbourhood and client number.", "t0": 31.32, "t1": 37.13, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "82 of 322 activity-years", "kicker": "The first lead", "sub": "same activity, year, age band, income band, race group, neighbourhood and client number"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 1.12, 1.96, 2.63, 3.33, 3.57, 4.12, 4.7, 4.95, 5.41]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[0]"], "text": "In other activity-years, a typical 3 percent of cells are even. Here, at least 95 percent.", "t0": 37.25, "t1": 43.81, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["the other activity-years", "a typical 3% of cells hold an even count"], "b": ["the 82", "at least 95%"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.29, 1.28, 1.42, 1.87, 2.05, 2.43, 2.55, 2.9, 3.04, 3.95, 4.45, 4.63, 5.04, 5.99]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why", "story[1]"], "text": "That is 10.6 percent of all the records, about one in ten.", "t0": 43.93, "t1": 48.49, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "10.6% of all 311,824 records", "sub": "second copies"}, "emph": ["one in ten"], "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.26, 0.56, 0.9, 1.2, 1.7, 1.92, 2.14, 2.33, 3.28, 3.6, 3.89, 4.18]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "s3", "s4"], "text": "Each year the office also reports these services to HUD, its federal funder.", "t0": 48.71, "t1": 53.08, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Annual reports to HUD (CAPER)", "kicker": "The second lead", "sub": "2017-18 and 2018-19"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.48, 0.66, 1.07, 1.37, 1.76, 2.02, 2.5, 2.68, 3.14, 3.36, 3.72]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "s3", "s4"], "text": "We matched the reports line by line. What do they print?", "t0": 53.2, "t1": 56.64, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Annual reports to HUD (CAPER)", "kicker": "The second lead", "sub": "2017-18 and 2018-19"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.05, 0.35, 0.47, 0.97, 1.35, 1.53, 2.08, 2.36, 2.45, 2.63]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "Exactly half, in 13 of 13 paired activity-years tested.", "t0": 56.64, "t1": 61.37, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "13 of 13", "label": "paired activity-years where the report prints exactly half", "sub": "and the full count in 10 of 10 unpaired controls"}, "emph": ["13 of 13"], "wt": [0.04, 0.59, 1.35, 1.53, 2.17, 2.4, 2.96, 3.43, 4.16]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "established[1]"], "text": "Where records are single, the report gives the full count, 10 of 10.", "t0": 61.89, "t1": 66.08, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["paired records", "the report prints half"], "b": ["records not paired", "the full count, 10 of 10"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.08, 0.45, 0.57, 1.09, 1.22, 1.67, 1.89, 2.02, 2.34, 3.09, 3.55, 3.93]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why", "established[2]"], "text": "So the report to the funder counts each person once. The open file counts some twice.", "t0": 66.2, "t1": 71.67, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Number of individuals …"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.25, 0.62, 0.69, 0.79, 1.19, 1.52, 1.77, 2.2, 2.95, 3.13, 3.47, 3.85, 4.25, 4.64]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "Service-connection case management logged 3,050 records in its last year. What did HUD hear?", "t0": 71.89, "t1": 78.25, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["case-management records, 2018-19", "3,050"], "b": ["individuals in the report to HUD", "1,525"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.72, 1.08, 1.59, 2.05, 2.39, 3.01, 3.35, 3.87, 3.98, 4.22, 4.53, 5.3, 5.4, 5.56, 5.74]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what"], "text": "1,525 people. Exactly half.", "t0": 78.25, "t1": 82.93, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "1,525", "label": "individuals receiving case management, 2018-19", "sub": "exactly half of 3,050"}, "emph": ["1,525"], "wt": [0.04, 0.56, 1.02, 1.44, 1.8, 2.67, 3.21, 4.22]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "suspicious[3].what"], "text": "Rental assistance to prevent eviction shows the same halving, year after year.", "t0": 83.45, "t1": 88.11, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["rental assistance records, 2015-16 to 2017-18", "1,534 · 1,086 · 924"], "b": ["individuals in the report to HUD", "767 · 543 · 462"], "kicker": "Rental assistance for eviction prevention"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.72, 0.86, 1.21, 1.76, 2.04, 2.18, 2.56, 3.38, 3.78, 4.25]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "suspicious[3].why"], "text": "Information and referral, whose records are single, matches the report one for one.", "t0": 88.23, "t1": 93.67, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["information and referral records, 2017-18", "3,677"], "b": ["in the report to HUD", "3,677"]}, "emph": ["one for one"], "wt": [0.0, 0.68, 0.86, 1.55, 2.12, 2.44, 2.62, 3.33, 3.7, 3.83, 4.36, 4.8, 5.1]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "suspicious[4].what"], "text": "The records name no provider, so nobody can trace the pairs to a grantee.", "t0": 93.89, "t1": 98.25, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "No provider named", "kicker": "The fourth lead", "sub": "111,120 records have no client number"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.62, 0.96, 1.18, 1.89, 2.05, 2.36, 2.53, 2.82, 2.96, 3.41, 3.56, 3.67]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "span", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "timeline[3]"], "text": "The file stops at fiscal 2018-19. It was last updated in May 2020.", "t0": 98.37, "t1": 104.05, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2016", "to": "2020-05-21", "days": "", "fromLab": "first fiscal year in the file", "toLab": "last update", "kicker": "stops at fiscal 2018-19"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.39, 0.77, 0.94, 1.33, 1.64, 2.13, 2.44, 3.23, 3.3, 3.42, 3.74, 4.21, 4.42, 4.77, 5.09]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "The records don’t say why the rows come in pairs.", "t0": 104.27, "t1": 107.49, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Why the rows are paired", "That any provider reported a service twice, or was paid twice for one"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.07, 0.46, 0.82, 1.16, 1.5, 1.7, 2.07, 2.31, 2.5]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["innocent[0]"], "text": "One row per funding source, or per reporting period, would pair them too.", "t0": 107.61, "t1": 111.73, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Why the rows are paired", "That any provider reported a service twice, or was paid twice for one"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.45, 0.68, 1.09, 1.56, 1.73, 1.96, 2.46, 3.14, 3.32, 3.54, 3.75]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it? How the office builds the file, and its counts by grantee.", "t0": 111.85, "t1": 116.37, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "How the office builds the public service records"}, {"who": "", "what": "Grantee-level service counts for fiscal 2015-16 to 2018-19"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.37, 0.69, 1.02, 1.48, 1.65, 1.97, 2.26, 2.4, 3.06, 3.16, 3.34, 3.73, 3.89]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status", "story[5]"], "text": "No regulator has ruled on it. The open file overstates services by about one in ten.", "t0": 116.49, "t1": 122.55, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.78, 1.0, 1.25, 1.41, 1.82, 2.53, 2.8, 3.18, 3.82, 4.37, 4.53, 4.88, 5.25, 5.6]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 122.67, "t1": 125.03, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.41, 0.56, 0.65, 1.36, 1.53, 1.7]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The question", "lead1": "Lead 1 · every record twice", "lead2": "Lead 2 · the reports to HUD", "lead3": "Lead 3 · the largest lines", "lead4": "Lead 4 · no provider, no new years", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "newsroom", "hook": "question"}